+### 0526 — Host VPN controller review requests production error-translation rework (TASK-260715-1rsqrh)
+- REVIEW: Focused controller/repository tests pass 57/57, focused TSan passes 23/23, full core validation passes 275/275, strict Swift format and diff checks pass, board validation passes, and both iOS/macOS adapter builds succeed when run sequentially.
+- REGRESSION: `IOSVPNHostSession.startTunnel` and `MacOSVPNHostSession.startTunnel` forward the public `NETunnelProviderSession.startTunnel(options:)` thrown `NSError` unchanged, while `VPNSessionController.performStart` maps only `VPNPreferencePlatformError` / `VPNPlatformError` and otherwise erases the real domain/code to reflected type plus code 0. The unit test injects a pre-normalized fake error, so the production adapter path is untested and cannot satisfy the accepted exact synchronous `NEVPNError` mapping.
+- REWORK: Normalize thrown NetworkExtension start errors at the thin adapter boundary (or through an equivalently shared injectable translator), preserve unknown domain/code, cover both iOS/macOS seams plus the disabled-manager production path, and rerun focused normal/TSan, full core, formatting/diff/board checks, and both adapter builds before another reviewer cycle.
+
+### 0511 — Host VPN control keeps system and provider authorities independent (TASK-260715-1rsqrh)
+- DECISION: `OwnedVPNManagerRepository` remains the only ownership/schema authority and now hands out a session only from a freshly loaded exact-owned current manager. `VPNSessionController` retains no manager cache or forwarding state; iOS/macOS wrappers retain the fresh manager only to keep its exact public `NETunnelProviderSession` alive for the command/observer lifetime.
+- ORDERING: Start and stop share one locked once-only stop claim, so cancellation, timeout, and a concurrent explicit stop cannot duplicate `stopTunnel`. Controller retirement cancels host waits and observers without claiming that stop; a cancelled stop waiter does not cancel the joined system-stop observation for other callers.
+- PROJECTION: Every non-connected system status clears capability immediately. A connected projection accepts only correlated, negotiated lifecycle/capability responses at one matching position strictly newer than the last accepted generation/sequence; relaunch starts without historical app state and asks the provider again. Non-running provider lifecycle states fail safe to zero capabilities.
+- ERROR CONTRACT: All 19 public `NEVPNConnectionError` codes, provider codes 1001–1009, unknown domains/codes, provider unknown codes, nil errors, and timeout/cancellation unavailability map to stable finite reasons while system status remains authoritative.
+- COVERAGE: Deterministic Swift Testing covers every status, exact v1 start options, synchronous errors, 60/15/3-second deadlines, cancellation/retirement, start-stop races, joined stops, initial observer races, deallocation, nil/late/wrong/corrupt/unsupported/mismatched/stale responses, generation reset, and app recreation.
+
 ### 0442 — Apple VPN terminal observation registers before authoritative status (TASK-260715-15vkvz)
 - REGRESSION: Both NetworkExtension adapters read `NEVPNConnection.status` before installing `NEVPNStatusDidChange`, so a terminal transition in that gap could be lost and an already-stopped session could falsely reach the 15-second `stopTimedOut` path.
 - FIX: iOS and macOS now install the observer first and then perform an authoritative status read through an injectable seam. The locked retirement handshake also handles a synchronous terminal notification before registration returns its token: completion wins once, and the late-arriving token is immediately unregistered.
